1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,700
What if you never slept again?

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,740
Good news: 8 free hours a day.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,840
Bad news: soon you'd see things that aren't there.

4
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:12,520
After just 24 hours awake, research says your brain works about as well as a drunk person's.

5
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:13,380
Zero drinks.

6
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:14,380
Fully wasted.

7
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:17,040
Then your brain stops asking permission.

8
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:19,920
Mid-conversation, it shuts off for a few seconds.

9
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:21,000
You won't even notice.

10
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,760
It's called a microsleep.

11
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:27,800
In 1964, a student named Randy Gardner stayed awake about 11 days.

12
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,960
By the end, he was seeing things and forgetting things.

13
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,640
And lab rats kept from sleeping?

14
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,500
They didn't make it past a few weeks.

15
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:35,400
One more thing.

16
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,780
If you're watching this at 2 AM…

17
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:38,380
subscribe first.

18
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:39,880
Then put the phone down…

19
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:40,900
and go to sleep.
